+# Tend UI Local Compensation Security
+
+## Status
+
+F-23 adds an executable policy for the three reviewed local compatibility packages used by S-Tracker: `classnames`, `lodash` and `uuid`.
+
+These packages are not downloaded from a closed registry. Their tarballs are stored in `vendor/tend-ui/`, resolve through `file:` references and remain marked `private` with `UNLICENSED` metadata.
+
+## Policy And Gate
+
+The machine-readable policy is `vendor/tend-ui/compensation-policy.json`. It records:
+
+- exact package versions and tarball names;
+- SHA-256 checksums;
+- allowed runtime exports;
+- deliberately absent upstream APIs;
+- the disposition of version-based audit signals.
+
+Run the security gate with:
+
+```powershell
+npm.cmd run verify:tend-ui:security
+```
+
+The script verifies the tarball checksum, `package.json` and lockfile source, private metadata, API allowlist and behavior related to the known signals.
+
+## Advisory Disposition
+
+| Package | Version-based signal | Local implementation evidence | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `lodash@4.17.21` | Upstream `template`, `unset` and deep-path `omit` behavior. | `template` and `unset` are absent. Local `omit` deletes direct own keys only; a regression test proves that it neither traverses a nested path nor changes `Object.prototype`. | Accepted as a reviewed local compensation. Recheck after every tarball change. |
+| `uuid@10.0.0` | Upstream namespace/buffer behavior in v3/v5/v6. | Only `v4` is exposed. It returns a UUID string and does not mutate a caller-supplied buffer. | Accepted as a reviewed local compensation. Recheck after every tarball change. |
+| `classnames@2.5.1` | No active F-22 signal. | Exact local tarball and export surface are pinned. | Keep inside the same integrity gate. |
+
+`npm audit fix` must not replace these packages automatically. A change is accepted only after policy, checksum and behavior tests are updated together.
+
+## Failure Policy
+
+Any checksum, source, metadata, export or behavior mismatch fails the gate. The correct response is to review the changed local implementation; the verifier must not be weakened merely to accept drift.
+
+## Verified Result
+
+On 2026-07-22 the gate passed for `3/3` local compensations. No network or corporate source was used.
